# Git LFS — large raw-CAN frame logs
#
# Policy (see docs/concepts/broadcast-frames.md → "Storing raw-CAN logs"):
#   • Our OWN captured logs (profiles/*/captures/can/**) are committed FULLY,
#     via LFS when large/binary.
#   • THIRD-PARTY logs are committed only when their license permits
#     redistribution (recorded alongside); unlicensed corpora (e.g. uhi22) stay
#     fetch-on-demand in the gitignored references/can/ + a tiny fair-use excerpt
#     under tests/fixtures/.
#
# Rules are last-match-wins: track the large binary frame-log formats by
# extension and everything under a profile's captures/can/, then explicitly
# UN-track the tiny committed test fixtures so they stay plain, diffable git.

# Binary / high-volume frame-log formats, wherever they live
*.blf filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.asc filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.trc filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text

# A profile's own raw-CAN capture store (any format, incl. large .csv logs)
profiles/*/captures/can/** filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text

# Diagnostic capture files (captures/YYYY-MM-DD.json) are append-only session
# logs — two machines routinely both append on the same day, which git's
# line-based merge conflicts on (and misaligns inside records) even though the
# data model is a trivially mergeable list. Route them through canair's
# session-union merge driver. Requires a one-time per-clone registration:
#   canair captures merge-driver --install
# (git never loads a driver command from a tracked file, for safety; until a
# clone installs it, merges simply fall back to normal conflict markers).
profiles/*/captures/*.json merge=canair-captures

# Keep the tiny hand-trimmed test fixtures in plain git (must stay diffable /
# inspectable; they are only KB-sized excerpts).
tests/fixtures/** !filter !diff !merge text=auto
